<Step ID="3" Task="For the chosen y, verify that for any distinct x_i, x_j in S₀, the inner product ⟨v_{x_i}, v_{x_j}⟩ = 0. Given that ∥x_i - x_j∥ = d and ∥x_i - y∥ = ∥x_j - y∥ = d/√2, compute ⟨x_i - y, x_j - y⟩. What is the result?" Difficulty="6" Token="70" Rely="2"/>
<Step ID="4" Task="Now consider any x in S (not necessarily in S₀). We need to show that ∥x - y∥ = d/√2. Using the fact that ∥x - x_i∥ = d for all x_i in S₀ and the parallelogram law, can we derive this?" Difficulty="7" Token="80" Rely="2,3"/>
<Step ID="5" Task="Finally, for any x in S and any x_i in S₀, show that ⟨v_x, v_{x_i}⟩ = 0. Using the result from Step 4 that ∥x - y∥ = d/√2 and the given ∥x - x_i∥ = d, compute ⟨x - y, x_i - y⟩. What is the value?" Difficulty="7" Token="80" Rely="3,4"/>
<Step ID="6" Task="Conclude that the set { (√2/d)(x - y) : x ∈ S } is an orthonormal system in ℋ, as all vectors have norm 1 and are pairwise orthogonal. Is this conclusion valid?" Difficulty="4" Token="50" Rely="5"/>
</Plan>
